msgid "Start increasing your revenue, customer loyalty and satisfaction with user-friendly emails based on order status."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Welcome/views/shopmagic_welcome-view.php:53
#: dist/admin/main.js:4014
msgid "Set up your automated email"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Welcome/views/shopmagic_welcome-view.php:57
msgid ""
"Each automation may consist of three elements: <b>Event</b> (e.g. <i>Order Completed</i>), which is a trigger.\n"
"\t\t\t\t\t\t<b>Filter</b> (e.g. <i>Order - Items</i>), which you can use if you want to send your email to selected group of customers and\n"
"\t\t\t\t\t\t<b>Action</b> (e.g. <i>Send Email</i>) in which you can create your message to the recipient."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Welcome/views/shopmagic_welcome-view.php:73
msgid "Start by creating a new <a href=\"%1$s\">Automation →</a> or choose one of the <a href=\"%2$s\">ready-to-use Recipes</a>."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Welcome/views/shopmagic_welcome-view.php:84
msgid "If you decide to create an automation from scratch, select an <b>Event</b> which will be a trigger for your automation. You can select from a variety of events, from <i>New Order</i> email, through <i>Order Pending</i> to <i>Order Completed</i>. We covered all of the WooCommerce order statuses."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Welcome/views/shopmagic_welcome-view.php:99
#: dist/admin/main.js:4019
msgid "Event setter for automation with Order Completed selected"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Welcome/views/shopmagic_welcome-view.php:105
msgid "Optionally - assign a <b>Filter</b>. Use it if you want to send your automation to the selected group of customers only."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Welcome/views/shopmagic_welcome-view.php:117
#: dist/admin/main.js:4020
msgid "Filter setter for automation with Order Items selected"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Welcome/views/shopmagic_welcome-view.php:123
msgid "Choose an <b>Action</b>. Select an Action type and enter data in action fields, as described. Do not forget to Publish your automation."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Welcome/views/shopmagic_welcome-view.php:135
#: dist/admin/main.js:4022
msgid "Action setter for automation with Send Email selected"
msgstr ""

